        ],
        correctIndex: 3,
        explanation: "Amylase is a biological enzyme catalyst (protein) that accelerates starch hydrolysis into sugars. Iron, Nickel, and Platinum are inorganic transition metal catalysts."
      },
      {
        id: 25,
        source: "Dr. AD Part",
        category: "catalysis",
        categoryName: "Catalysis",
        question: "The phenomenon in which a catalyst becomes temporarily inactive because another substance strongly adsorbs on its active sites is called:",
        options: [
          "Autocatalysis",
          "Catalyst poisoning",
          "Promoter action",
